From: Wolfram Huesken <woh@m18.io>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 09:13:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 04/14] fix(agent): operator artifact shapes, target-facing
 bash progress, honest run labels
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Patches 8-10 of the local vigolium stack, on top of 77725f2a (patches 1-7 plus
the re-apply guide) which sits on 82a92a92 (v0.5.3). Per-patch symptoms, root
causes, anchors and recipes live in docs/development/local-agent-pipeline-patches.md;
the config side (needed to reproduce behaviour, and not in git) is listed there
under "Config side (not in git)".

8. Artifact shapes — pkg/agent/autopilot_context.go
   countEvidenceBackedFindings accepted only an array of objects or
   {"findings":[...]}. The operator writes dismissed.json as a flat array of
   ruled-out reasons (plain strings), so a complete run ended with
   "failed to parse dismissed.json as findings artifact". Entries may now be any
   JSON value: string entries count where no evidence check applies (the
   dismissed artifact) and stay flagged as evidence-free in findings.json.
   Test: TestCountEvidenceBackedFindingsAcceptsPlainStringEntries.

9. Target-facing bash counts as progress — pkg/olium/autopilot/rotation.go,
   pkg/olium/autopilot/autopilot.go
   The stall detector's productiveTools is a static tool-name set, so an operator
   that verifies through the shell (curl with a harvested session cookie,
   replaying a captured request) looked stalled: two rotations at 12 turns then a
   halt, with ~36 turns of real probing discarded. productiveCall now also counts
   a bash call whose command names an HTTP client (curl/wget/httpie/httpx/hurl/
   ncat/netcat) and an in-scope host; progressTargetHosts derives the hosts from
   the target + scope and includes loopback aliases. EventToolExecEnd carries no
   args, so the loop stashes ToolArgs at EventToolExecStart and decides at end.
   Source reads, URL greps and `docker exec mysql` still count as no progress.
   Tests: TestProductiveCall, TestProgressTargetHosts,
   TestRunCountsTargetFacingBashAsProgress, TestRunStillStallsOnNonTargetBash.

10. A finished run does not read as broken — pkg/cli/agent_session.go,
    pkg/agent/autopilot_context.go
    (a) A warned run keeps its warning list in the same field a failed run keeps
        its error, and the session detail hard-coded an "Error" heading, so a
        successful 7h45m run with 13 findings read as failed. runMessageLabel now
        follows the status ("Warnings" vs "Error"), for parent and child runs.
    (b) hasEvidence only accepted inlined evidence, so findings citing linked
        HTTP records counted as evidence-free ("19 entries without evidence
        references" for a run where 7 of the 19 had linked records). Non-empty
        http_record_uuids / evidence_record_uuids now count, including []string.
    Tests: TestRunMessageLabel, plus the reference-list cases in
    TestHasEvidenceRecognisesWhiteboxProvenance. Against that run's real
    artifact the counter went from count=6 / 19 unsupported to 13 / 12.

Re-applying on a fresh clone
  git format-patch 82a92a92..HEAD -o <dir>     # in this repo
  cd <fresh clone> && git am <dir>/*.patch     # applies ce8fcf20, 77725f2a, this
or: git cherry-pick ce8fcf20 77725f2a <this-commit>
Then: make test-unit && make build, and apply the config-side settings from the
guide. Verify a patch is present with the anchor greps in that guide's "Checking
whether a newer release already has a fix" section.
